At wave1 still because player not shooting. We can use eval to kill and progress. Write async JS carefully. Since evaluate likely stringified. Use:
```
async () => {
 const g=__zeroHour;
 const sleepFrames=(n)=>new Promise(res=>{let i=0; const f=()=>{ if(++i>=n) res(); else requestAnimationFrame(f)}; requestAnimationFrame(f)});
 const log=[];
 for(let guard=0; guard<30; guard++){
   if(g.mode==='victory'||g.mode==='dead') break;
   g.spawnQueue.length=0;
   for(const e of [...g.enemies.enemies]) if(!e.dead) g.enemies.damage(e,99999,'head',e.root.position.clone(), {x:0,y:0,z:1});
   await sleepFrames(6);
   log.push({wave:g.wave,state:g.waveState,mode:g.mode,alive:g.enemies.aliveCount(),score:g.score});
   if(g.waveState==='intermission'){ g.intermissionT=0.001; await sleepFrames(4); }
   if(g.mode==='victory') break;
 }
 return log;
}
```
Careful passing plain object as dir to effects.blood clone methods? enemy.damage passes dir to effects.blood which calls dir.clone() - plain object fails. Need use existing Vector3; can get `new e.root.position.constructor(0,0,1)`? But THREE isn't global. Could use `g.forward.set(0,0,1)` (Vector3). Use `g.forward`. Or call `g.enemies.damage(e,99999,'body', e.root.position.clone(), g.forward.set(0,0,1))`. body zone no head; fine. This triggers onKill. Use e.root.position.clone().setY+1 maybe. Good.

Need kill final boss and minions. StartWave automatically sets queue but we set queue=[] immediately on each loop. Boss might not spawn. On final wave n=8, startWave puts boss in spawnQueue; our loop empties it. Then no boss, wave ends, finishRun(true) but win text "WARDEN NEUTRALIZED" though boss didn't spawn. Fine for flow testing. But to test boss, could spawn manually. Later.

